cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Sunflower-Formal: a machine-checked Coq account of the Erdős–Rado sunflower problem"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Falk"
    given-names: "Thomas"
    alias: "thomas-falk-research"
keywords:
  - Coq
  - formal verification
  - sunflower lemma
  - Erdős–Rado
  - Hall's marriage theorem
  - Kőnig's theorem
  - combinatorics
  - spread families
  - Alweiss-Lovett-Wu-Zhang
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked Coq (8.18, stdlib-only) proofs of the Erdős–Rado
  sunflower upper bound, the matching exponential lower bound
  f(n,k) >= (k-1)^n + 1, the exact value f(2,3) = 7, and constructive
  Hall and Kőnig theorems. The deterministic half of the 2020
  Alweiss-Lovett-Wu-Zhang / Rao spread argument is formalised: the
  reduction "every r-spread family of small sets has k pairwise
  disjoint members implies f(n,k) <= r^n + 1" is proved, and yields an
  unconditional bound f(n,k) <= (n(k-1)+1)^n + 1 when instantiated
  with an elementary spread lemma proved here. The open Sunflower
  Conjecture is stated formally, and the single axiom in the
  development is the published 2020 spread lemma, cited and used only
  by the one theorem explicitly derived from it.
